ober to November came in under 90% of normal in 35 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 5 grids. In 2025, that same pair came in at 35% of normal on the middle, while May to June ran 178%. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, at 57% or 58% of normal. On grid 15184, July to August 2026 sits at a preliminary estimate of 84.0 from NOAA rain.</p>"}
